    "details": "amqp091-go developers report:\n\n> Before version 1.13.0, a compromised or malicious AMQP broker can\n> force the client to allocate resources for and process content body\n> frames that exceed the negotiated frame_max limit. This can lead to\n> unexpected memory consumption or application-layer denial of service\n> (DoS), bypassing the protocol\\'s built-in framing constraints.\n\nRedpanda Connect vendored an affected amqp091-go release up to version\n4.108.0; 4.109.0 bumps it to 1.14.0.\n",
